  "slug": "east",
  "name": "EAST",
  "shortName": null,
  "description": "EAST, or EAST-CON, is an annual furry convention in Eastern Germany organized by Sachsen Furs e.V. It was created after the nature-preserve site of the camping event Tropicon was permanently closed, when several East German events agreed to combine into one convention. The name is an acronym for \"Episches Abfeiern Streunender Tiere\", or \"Epic Partying of Straying Animals\". The first EAST was held September 8 to 11, 2011, at the Youth Hostel Nebra, and it later moved to Falkenstein in the Harz Mountains, the Hostel Dessau-Rosslau and, from 2017, the Ringberg Hotel in Suhl. Attendance grew from 36 to 948 in 2025, and each edition has a theme and a local charity.",
